From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: gunyah: ROG5: run the Haven watchdog

The ROG Phone 5 runs Qualcomm's Haven hypervisor, whose virtual watchdog
has the same SMCCC interface as the Gunyah watchdog. qcom_scm never
registers the gunyah-wdt device there: Haven reports SMCCC 1.0, so the
hypervisor UID query that identifies Gunyah is not available. Register it
on this machine anyway; the driver's probe still requires a working
STATUS call.

Set the bark 3 s before the bite, as the downstream Haven driver did.
With bark == bite Haven flags the watchdog as expired the moment it is
enabled, and one such test (an idle phone for two minutes) ended with the
watchdog disabled and no bite.

Start the watchdog at probe on this machine and mark it running, so the
watchdog core pets it until user space opens the device: a hard hang
during boot then resets the phone too. Haven counts only busy time (it
keeps the watchdog petted while all CPUs idle), so it catches spinning
CPUs and stalled bus accesses, not an all-idle deadlock. Stop and restart
it across system suspend in that state as well.

Tested with the driver as a module on 7.2.7 r62: 45 s of full load with
the core petting (at most 15.4 s between pets), then stop_machine() with
interrupts off on every CPU; Haven reset the phone within 41 s and it
booted the default image by itself.

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2493,9 +2493,15 @@
 		"arm,sbsa-gwdt",
 	};
 
-	/* Bail out if we are not running under Gunyah */
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY) ||
-	    !arm_smccc_hypervisor_has_uuid(&gunyah_uuid))
+	/*
+	 * Bail out if we are not running under Gunyah. The Haven release on
+	 * the ROG Phone 5 reports SMCCC 1.0, so the hypervisor UID query is
+	 * not available there, but its watchdog calls are; the watchdog
+	 * driver's probe checks them before it registers anything.
+	 */
+	if ((!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY) ||
+	     !arm_smccc_hypervisor_has_uuid(&gunyah_uuid)) &&
+	    !of_machine_is_compatible("asus,rog-phone5"))
 		return;
 
 	/*
--- a/drivers/watchdog/gunyah_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/gunyah_wdt.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/watchdog.h>
 
@@ -64,7 +65,7 @@
 
 static int gunyah_wdt_start(struct watchdog_device *wdd)
 {
-	unsigned int timeout_ms;
+	unsigned int timeout_ms, bark_ms;
 	struct device *dev = wdd->parent;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -74,8 +75,14 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Bark before the bite, as the Haven driver on SM8350 did (bite =
+	 * bark + 3 s). With bark == bite, Haven reports the watchdog as
+	 * expired as soon as it is enabled.
+	 */
 	timeout_ms = wdd->timeout * 1000;
-	ret = gunyah_wdt_call(GUNYAH_WDT_SET_TIME, timeout_ms, timeout_ms);
+	bark_ms = timeout_ms > 6000 ? timeout_ms - 3000 : timeout_ms / 2;
+	ret = gunyah_wdt_call(GUNYAH_WDT_SET_TIME, bark_ms, timeout_ms);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: Failed to set timeout for gunyah wdt %d\n",
 			__func__, ret);
@@ -196,6 +203,17 @@
 	wdd->timeout = wdd->max_timeout;
 
 	gunyah_wdt_stop(wdd);
+
+	/*
+	 * On the ROG Phone 5, run the watchdog from probe on and let the
+	 * watchdog core pet it until user space opens the device, so that a
+	 * hard hang during boot (CPUs spinning, a stalled bus access) resets
+	 * the phone too. Haven counts only busy time: it keeps the watchdog
+	 * petted while all CPUs idle.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,rog-phone5") && !gunyah_wdt_start(wdd))
+		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdd->status);
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, wdd);
 	watchdog_set_restart_priority(wdd, 0);
 
@@ -213,7 +231,7 @@
 {
 	struct watchdog_device *wdd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(wdd))
+	if (watchdog_active(wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(wdd))
 		gunyah_wdt_stop(wdd);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -223,7 +241,7 @@
 {
 	struct watchdog_device *wdd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(wdd))
+	if (watchdog_active(wdd) || watchdog_hw_running(wdd))
 		gunyah_wdt_start(wdd);
 
 	return 0;
